Package: vabaxos-unlock
Architecture: all
Maintainer: VabaxOS <https://github.com/Vabax-dev/VabaxOS>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: initramfs-tools, espeak-ng, alsa-utils, kmod
Enhances: cryptsetup-initramfs
Description: A voice when the computer asks the password of the disk
 With an encrypted disk, the computer asks its password at boot, before
 any screen reader can start: a blind person hears only silence. With
 vabaxos-unlock the initramfs plays two tones and says "Type the password
 of the disk, then press Enter", then "Wrong password" or "Disk open", in
 the language and at the speed of the system (ADR-0021). Debian's own
 prompt reads the password as always. Nothing changes on systems without
 encrypted disks.
